            <div xml:id="d51">

                <pb facs="0059" n="50" sameAs="frus:frus1938v05/pg50"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">710.H Continental Solidarity/55: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in Venezuela</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Gonzalez</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary
                        of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Caracas</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1938-12-08T20:00:00-04:30">December 8, 1938—8
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received 8:17 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>113. Only for the President. Following information confidentially learned from
                    the Minister of Foreign Relations conveyed herein to you directly because of its
                    immediate importance and because your leadership and counteraction are as they
                    have been manifestly the only effective instruments to overcome opposition and
                    to sustain the success of the Latin American policy established by you.</p>
                <pb facs="0060" n="51" xml:id="pg51"/>
                <p>Was informed that German and Italian observers are to be at Lima Conference to
                    spread influence action against questions of defense, etc. and to oppose any
                    success by us at the Conference by creation of a bloc. The Minister for Foreign
                    Affairs showed me a cabled instruction to the Venezuelan delegation instructing
                    it to cooperate in every way with the delegations of the United States and of
                    Brazil and further that on controversial questions no opposition in open debate
                    should be made to the position taken by the above mentioned countries,
                    differences if any to be discussed privately with a view to reaching amicable
                    agreements.</p>
                <p>Have advised Secretary Hull at Lima.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Gonzalez</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
